Does anyone have a public domain version of date?  I've implemented
a version of localtime that I got over the net which seems to work
quite well with the new time change.  Since we don't have system
source there are a number of other programs that don't know the
correct local time, how-ever we do need a correct GMT, so changing
the system clock would mess up the machine's idea of GMT.

Anyhow I'd like to put the routines into a System V type date(1)
so that programs and scripts that call that program will get a good
date/time.

The joys of a binary license.  If I only had an extra ~$40K for a
source license.

